WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.100
Good morning, Hank. It's Tuesday.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.631
Today is the ninth day of Pizzamas, so to
celebrate, today’s video comes to you in

00:00:05.631 --> 00:00:07.031
nine very special parts.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.280
That was part one, the intro.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.600
Part Two: Unabashed Promotion of Saleable
Goods.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:14.550
So there are only a few days left to order
all your Pizzamas stuff from dftba.com.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:18.160
All these beautiful Pizza John shirts and
the Pizza John PJs and everything else is

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:20.350
only available ‘til the end of Pizzamas.

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:21.760
Part Three: Good News.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:25.710
So I don’t want to minimize or ignore the
torrent of bad news currently washing over

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:30.170
the world, but I did want to call your attention
to one piece of extraordinarily good news

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:31.780
that I think has gone underreported.

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:35.920
It’s just been announced that global carbon
emissions are expected to be nearly flat in

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:40.380
2016, marking the third straight year of no
carbon emission growth.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:41.400
That’s really good news.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:45.000
Unfortunately, it’s not good enough news,
because emissions are still far too high

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.190
to limit post-industrial warming to below
two degrees celsius.

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:52.410
But it’s important because it underscores
that humanity can reach its other goals without

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:53.430
increasing emissions.

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:57.720
Like, the global economy grew by about 3%
this year, and both poverty and disease burden

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:58.690
were reduced.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:00.000
Part Three (four): Bad News.

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:04.659
The UN has just reported that 2016 will almost
certainly be the hottest year in recorded

00:01:04.659 --> 00:01:05.599
human history.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:09.300
And worrisomely, that record will likely only
stand until 2017.

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:13.700
Climate change is real, humans are causing
it, and the people of the future will judge

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:15.500
us on how we dealt with it.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:16.820
Part Five: More Good News.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:20.819
AFC Wimbledon, the fan-owned English soccer
team who wear DFTBA on their shorts have had

00:01:20.819 --> 00:01:25.279
an astonishingly successful first season in
the third tier of English football.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:28.860
Seventeen games into the season, they are
just three points from a playoff spot, while

00:01:28.861 --> 00:01:32.721
the franchise currently playing in Milton
Keynes is in the relegation zone.

00:01:32.721 --> 00:01:36.139
All of this is just further proof that we
are living in the best sports timeline of

00:01:36.139 --> 00:01:39.559
the entire multiverse, and also the worst
everything else timeline.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:42.359
Part Six: Unabashed Promotion of Saleable
Goods.

00:01:42.359 --> 00:01:46.229
While you’re over at dftba.com picking up
this comfortable and fashionable Pizza John

00:01:46.229 --> 00:01:49.229
hoodie, why not buy an AFC WImbledon Nerdfighteria
scarf?

00:01:49.229 --> 00:01:52.259
All proceeds go to the club, and maybe if
we sell enough scarves, they will make it

00:01:52.259 --> 00:01:55.399
back to the playoffs, and I will get to go
to Wembley and feel like this again.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.300
Part Seven: More Bad News.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:00.250
So Hank, one of my favorite songwriters, Leonard
Cohen, died last week.

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:05.000
He was everything I wanna be when I grow up:
empathetic and smart without ever being condescending

00:02:05.009 --> 00:02:08.649
or cold, and he also gave me one the central
ideas in my book Paper Towns.

00:02:08.649 --> 00:02:12.099
I’m gonna put a link to some of my favorite
Leonard Cohen songs in the dooblydoo below

00:02:12.099 --> 00:02:13.099
for you to enjoy.

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:14.489
Part Eight: More Good News.

00:02:14.489 --> 00:02:17.729
Amid loss, there is still great art being
made in the world.

00:02:17.729 --> 00:02:21.060
Quick side story, when I was fifteen, I wrote
this extremely sincere and terrible paper

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:24.700
for English about how there could never be
another great work of fiction because Dostoyevsky

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:25.380
was dead.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:28.720
And then like four months later, we read Toni
Morrison’s Song of Solomon, and Tony

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:32.219
Kushner’s Angels in America, and I was like,
“Oh, oh, okay.

00:02:32.219 --> 00:02:34.019
I would like to file a retraction.”

00:02:34.019 --> 00:02:37.540
Anyway, twenty years later, Dostoyevsky is
still dead and there are still truly great

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:38.460
books being written.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:42.720
Most recently I had been completely astonished
by this book: What Is Not Yours Is Not Yours,

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:46.640
but I’ll have many more book recommendations
in my forthcoming holiday gift book roundup.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:50.640
In the meantime, if there are books that you
would suggest to me, please do so in comments.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:51.160
Thanks.

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:52.600
Part Nine: The Outtro.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.819
So I think I’m gonna close out my part of
Pizzamas on Thursday with an old-fashioned

00:02:55.819 --> 00:02:58.539
Question Tuesday, because, you know, what
better day to do it?

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:02.420
So please leave your questions, ideally brief
ones in the comment section below.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:05.230
And I thought I’d leave you today with some
of my favorite Leonard Cohen lines:

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:07.560
Ring the bells that still can ring.

00:03:07.569 --> 00:03:09.560
Forget your perfect offering.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:12.140
There’s a crack in everything.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:14.180
That’s how the light gets in.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:15.180
Endscreen!

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:18.840
Oh look it’s that book that I liked and
Pizzamas merch and a couple of my favorite

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:23.000
Leonard Cohen songs and perhaps most importantly,
a bunny from Rosianna.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.680
Self-Care Bunny is here to remind you to take
care of yourself because there is only one

00:03:26.689 --> 00:03:28.579
of you, and the world is lucky to have you.

